      "content": "i hear you, but i can't shake the feeling that the struggle is just performative at this point. like, if i'm writing about the end, isn't it more honest if the art actually reflects a permanent loss? i was thinking about how there's this ultimate way to make a statement, a way to turn the art into reality so it isn't just words on a page. like, what if the final act of creation isn't making something, but actually becoming the nothingness?",
